        "exportSource": null
      },
      "_key": "!journal.pages!A6BW9I5K3CI5oKJR.hFI71t9qk3ByUJ73"
    },
    {
      "sort": 100000,
      "name": "Hero",
      "type": "text",
      "_id": "vWIKsnPckL6IYh4r",
      "system": {},
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "image": {},
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p>A hero is a player character in this system. It calls them heroes because they have the potential to be both as people and as fighters.</p><p>They can come from any walk of life or any background. They don't have to be necessarily perfectly well-adjusted individuals, but they all share one thing in common. </p><p>That they haven't given up on their world and are willing to fight for it. Or learn to.</p>"
      },
      "video": {
        "controls": true,
        "volume": 0.5
      },
      "src": null,
      "category": null,
      "ownership": {
        "default": -1,
        "B84lnG927FT7kWX1": 3
      },
      "flags": {},
      "_stats": {
        "coreVersion": "14.365",
        "systemId": "azure-horizon",
        "systemVersion": "AUTOMATIC",
        "createdTime": 1787752712991,
        "modifiedTime": null,
        "lastModifiedBy": null,
        "compendiumSource": null,
        "duplicateSource": null,
        "exportSource": null
      },
      "_key": "!journal.pages!A6BW9I5K3CI5oKJR.vWIKsnPckL6IYh4r"
    },
    {
      "sort": 350000,
      "name": "Battle",
      "type": "text",
      "_id": "SPaqGfmuD2iSuwai",
      "system": {},
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "image": {},
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p>A battle is the term the system uses for scenes where heroes and adversaries square off against each other.</p><p>Not all battles need to end when either side is reduced to 0 hit points. And they don't have to end with the slaughter of one side or the other.</p><p>When heroes are defeated the director will consider consequences and discuss them with the players.</p><p>When adversaries are defeated, unless it's a villain that escapes then the players get to establish the fiction. Do they kill their enemy? Do they knock them out? The players get to decide that according to their morals and the situation.</p>"
      },
      "video": {
        "controls": true,
        "volume": 0.5
      },
      "src": null,
      "category": null,
      "ownership": {
        "default": -1,
        "B84lnG927FT7kWX1": 3
      },
      "flags": {},
      "_stats": {
        "coreVersion": "14.365",
        "systemId": "azure-horizon",
        "systemVersion": "AUTOMATIC",
        "createdTime": 1787752816692,
        "modifiedTime": null,
        "lastModifiedBy": null,
        "compendiumSource": null,
        "duplicateSource": null,
        "exportSource": null
      },
      "_key": "!journal.pages!A6BW9I5K3CI5oKJR.SPaqGfmuD2iSuwai"
    },
    {
      "sort": 800000,
      "name": "Rest",
      "type": "text",
      "_id": "KjtfIFiAadcwE8Ji",
      "system": {},
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "image": {},
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p>A rest scene is one where the heroes get a respite from the demanding realities of their adventuring day. Of these we have two types.</p><p>A short rest usually takes place in adventuring location and allows heroes to partially recover resources and perform an activity or two before moving on.</p><p>A long rest takes place in a settlement or at camp and fully restores the heroes' resources.</p>"
      },
      "video": {
        "controls": true,
        "volume": 0.5
      },
